features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:14:- Read `docs/spec.md` §11 (all of it: the table, "Consumables", "Preventing runaway leaders"), §3 (ruins), §16 (idempotent requests) and `docs/objectives.md`.
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:17:- Other features run at the same time and own the sea, server, web and tests, plus `packages/*/src/ruins` and `packages/*/src/intel`. Stay inside your owned paths.
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:27:- **Minted gold.** `grantGold(state, { playerId, reason, sourceKey, tick })`, with `reason` either `ruin` (40 gold) or `supply-cache` (25 gold); the amounts come from content.
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:29:  - It is idempotent by its key: a `ruin` grant is once per (player, `sourceKey`), where the ruin id is the key; a `supply-cache` grant is once per `sourceKey` for the whole match (one global claim, §11).
features/ledger-economy/ledger-task.md:49:   - a ruin grant once per player per ruin; a second player gets their own; a repeat is refused with the same state;
